#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Applying for credit with a freeze.</strong> Lift it at both bureaus "
"first. Equifax lets you suspend the lock for a period, then locks again by "
"itself. At TransUnion, a suspension with an end date is announced from July "
"1, 2027; until then a lifted freeze is not restored automatically: add a "
"reminder to put it back."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Costs.</strong> Every right is free, except the freeze, for which "
"the law allows reasonable fees (ss. 15 and 18). In practice the freeze is "
"free in Quebec (AMF), and neither bureau charges for it (Equifax, "
"TransUnion). Using a right cannot lower your score (s. 16)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Delays.</strong> The law refers to a delay set by government "
"regulation (ss. 22 and 23); none of the three regulations under the Act sets"
" it (LégisQuébec, up to date June 10, 2026). The bureaus announce: Equifax, "
"immediate online or by phone, up to five business days by mail; TransUnion, "
"immediate online or by phone, up to 30 days by mail."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Duration.</strong> The law sets none: a measure ends when you revoke"
" it (s. 12). A freeze stays until you lift it (Equifax, TransUnion). An "
"alert stays six years at Equifax and at TransUnion: your reminders plan its "
"renewal. To change the phone number of an Equifax alert, write with proof of"
" identity and a phone bill."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Equifax</strong>: online with a my.equifax.ca account, free, updated"
" monthly; Equifax says this data is stored in the United States. By phone: "
"1-800-465-7166 (automated, asks for your SIN; mailed in 5 to 10 days). By "
"mail: the request form with copies of two valid government ID, one showing "
"your current address, to Equifax Canada, Relations nationales avec les "
"consommateurs, C. P. 190, Montréal (Québec) H1S 2Z2."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Explanatory note</strong> (ss. 11 and 20): your side of a "
"disagreement with the bureau on access to or correction of your file; it "
"describes the disagreement and must not be defamatory."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>How.</strong> The request comes from you (or your representative), "
"with proof of identity; it can be made orally, except for an explanatory "
"note (s. 17). The bureau must agree to a compliant request and answer in "
"writing, with its reasons and your recourses if it refuses (ss. 21 and 22). "
"Online: from your Equifax or TransUnion account (AMF)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Recourse.</strong> If the bureau refuses: ask the Commission d'accès"
" à l'information to examine the disagreement (s. 24). If it does not answer "
"in time or does not follow through: complain to the Autorité des marchés "
"financiers, 1-877-525-0337 (s. 25; AMF)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Security alert</strong> (s. 10): whoever receives your file must "
"take reasonable steps to make sure it is really you before contracting, and "
"gets the phone number you gave, which the request must include (s. 19; "
"private sector act, s. 19.1)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>Security freeze</strong> (s. 9): the bureau may not share your file "
"to open credit, raise a credit limit, sign a long-term lease of goods (a car"
" lease, for example) or a remote service contract (a cell phone plan, for "
"example). Employers, collection agencies, governments, landlords and "
"insurers can still see the file with your permission (AMF)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"<strong>TransUnion</strong>: online at ocs.transunion.ca, a free consumer "
"disclosure every month; for Quebec and Ontario residents it includes the "
"score and its factors. By phone: 1-800-663-9980. By mail: the consumer "
"request form with copies (front and back) of two ID that together show your "
"name, current address, date of birth and signature, to TransUnion, Consumers"
" Relations Department, 3115 Harvester Road, Suite 201, Burlington, ON L7N "
"3N8."
msgstr ""

