" history: your identity, your loans and cards and how you repay them, your "
"bank accounts and NSF cheques, unpaid accounts, public records (bankruptcy, "
"judgment), who asked to see your file, and your score (AMF)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"Your <strong>credit score</strong> is a number between 300 and 900 computed "
"from the file; the higher, the better. There is no single score: lenders "
"receive other scores than the one you get, but they tend toward the same "
"value (AMF). Scores are updated at least once a month (FCAC)."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_credit_identity
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:bf_credit_identity.credit_guide_content
msgid ""
"Your SIN is not an ID: give it only when the law requires it. It is not "
"needed to apply for a credit card, rent a home or get your credit report "
"(Service Canada)."
